Subject: [PATCH] Preserve format checks in extra-module compiler flags

OpenVINO 2026.2.0 appends -Wno-all for extra modules. Fedora 44 supplies
-Werror=format-security, which requires -Wformat. GCC 16.2.1 consequently
rejects even safe C/C++ source before compilation in the NPU compiler.
Keep format checking enabled without removing Fedora's security error flag.

Regression: check-format-security.py invokes this actual macro in a CMake
project: safe C/C++ must compile and unsafe printf calls must fail specifically
on -Werror=format-security. The retained build's failed NPU object commands
provide the integration reproduction.

--- a/cmake/developer_package/compile_flags/functions.cmake
+++ b/cmake/developer_package/compile_flags/functions.cmake
@@ -43,7 +43,8 @@
 #
 macro(ov_dev_package_no_errors)
     if(OV_COMPILER_IS_CLANG OR CMAKE_COMPILER_IS_GNUCXX OR (OV_COMPILER_IS_INTEL_LLVM AND UNIX))
-        set(ov_c_cxx_dev_no_errors "-Wno-all")
+        # Preserve format checking required by distro -Werror=format-security.
+        set(ov_c_cxx_dev_no_errors "-Wno-all -Wformat")
         if(SUGGEST_OVERRIDE_SUPPORTED)
             set(ov_cxx_dev_no_errors "-Wno-error=suggest-override")
         endif()
